    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green. Here's what I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded an optional `postcode` (4 digits) to owners, validated against the city's region only when present, and stored/returned when supplied \u2014 keeping the request contract backward-compatible.\n\n**Region rule:** derived from the existing city\u2192region table (`Sydney`\u2192NSW, `Melbourne`\u2192VIC, `Brisbane`\u2192QLD). Ranges: NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099. A city with no known region (`UNKNOWN`) accepts any 4-digit postcode. Malformed or out-of-range \u2192 **400**; absent \u2192 accepted.\n\n**Files changed:**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added `postcode` to `OwnerFields` (optional, not in `required`), which regenerates the DTO getter/setter that MapStruct maps automatically in both directions.\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 new `postcode` column + accessors.\n- DB schemas (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 new `postcode` column; the positional `hsqldb/data.sql` seed rows got a matching `NULL`.\n- New `function/owner/Postcode.java` \u2014 the validation helper (format + region-range check, mirroring the existing `Locality` table).\n- New `function/owner/RequirePostcode.java` \u2014 the pipeline step; skips when absent.\n- New escalation `InvalidPostcodeException` + handler + YAML \u2192 responds 400 as a `ProblemDetail`, matching the existing `InvalidTelephoneException` convention.\n- Wired `RequirePostcode` into `owners.POST.yml` (after `require`) and `owners/{ownerId}.PUT.yml` (after `validate`); `ApplyOwner` now persists postcode on update.\n\n**Design note:** the POST pipeline's first step binds `@RequestBody` *without* `@Valid`, so the OpenAPI `pattern` alone wouldn't reject a malformed postcode on create \u2014 hence the explicit `RequirePostcode` step rather than relying on bean validation.\n\n**Verification:** the full suite (`mvn test`) passes \u2014 the three new acceptance tests (`coreStoresValidPostcode`, `coreAcceptsOwnerWithoutPostcode`, `errorRejectsMalformedPostcode`) plus a temporary test I added and then removed that confirmed out-of-range rejection, valid-in-region storage, and permissive unknown-region acceptance.",
